                <pb facs="0544" n="456" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg456"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/2984: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grant-Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Copenhagen</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-13T18:00:00+01:00"
                            >December 13, 1918—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3298. My 3246, December 4th, 6 p.m.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d397-f1"/> Danish
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs, under date of 12th, instant,<anchor n="13"
                        xml:id="d397-f2"/> states that the French Minister has informed him that his
                    Government had suggested that if Denmark desired to have the question of the
                    recovery of North Schleswig taken up at the Peace Conference, an official
                    request in that sense should be made to the Associated Governments. M.
                    Scavenius, therefore, makes the formal request that the Peace Conference should
                    take this matter under consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant-Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
